country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAITO KINSHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARA, HIDEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAITO, KINSHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A rotary servo valve (1) comprising at least two types of high and low pressure pump ports (33, 39), wherein a rotatable and linearly reciprocating spool (11) is installed through a spool guide hole (7) in a valve main body (9), a servo motor (15) drivingly rotating the spool and a linear actuator (13) reciprocatingly moving it are provided, whereby the pump ports can be switched selectively by the reciprocating movement of the spool and the cylinder ports can be switched selectively and flow rate can be controlled by the rotation.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une servovalve rotative (1) comprenant au moins deux types d'orifices de pompe haute et basse pression (33, 39), un tiroir cylindrique rotatif à mouvement de va-et-vient linéaire (11) étant installé dans un orifice de guidage (7) ménagé sur le corps principal (9) de la valve. Un servomoteur (15) est par ailleurs destiné à entraîner ce tiroir cylindrique afin de lui imprimer un mouvement de rotation, et un actionneur linéaire (13) à lui faire adopter un mouvement de va-et-vient, les orifices de la pompe pouvant être sélectivement obturés par ce mouvement de va-et-vient du tiroir cylindrique, et le débit régulé par le mouvement de rotation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>